  "market_context": "AUDUSD was in a clear daily downtrend with lower highs and lower lows. Price broke the descending trendline temporarily, causing a false breakout, before sharply rejecting at the key psychological level 0.7100 with a strong bearish candle.",
  "key_observation": "Price formed a lower high at ~0.7100 while RSI showed a higher high—classic bearish hidden divergence—confirming trend continuation despite the trendline break.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified the daily downtrend using lower highs and lower lows, and drew a descending trendline connecting prior swing highs.",
    "Step 2: Noted price broke the downtrend line but then rejected aggressively at the 0.7100 psychological level with a large bearish candle (100-pip daily candle).",
    "Step 3: Observed the three-line strike candlestick pattern forming at 0.7100, signaling strong bearish momentum continuation.",
    "Step 4: Compared RSI peaks at the two recent highs: the second price high (~0.7100) was lower than the prior high, but the RSI peak was higher—confirming bearish hidden divergence.",
    "Step 5: Entered a short trade at 0.7100 with stop loss above the candle’s high, targeting the previous swing low to recoup prior losses."
  ],
  "outcome": "The short trade recouped losses from the earlier stopped-out trade and allowed further profit by holding through lower-timeframe lower lows and lower highs.",
  "lessons": "Hidden divergences on HTF (daily) are high-probability trend continuation signals—even after false breakouts. Confluence of round number (0.7100), candlestick pattern (three-line strike), and RSI hidden divergence creates robust entry setup.",
